casts.verse_english:
— Four alone, and a single three: this it declares. —
Fleeing enmity and malice you shall come at last to your prize;
you shall come, and the grey-eyed goddess Athena will save you;
and the plan you set your hand to shall be after your heart.

— One falling four, and four ones in a row. —
Do not do the deed that you are doing, for it is not for the better;
and for one who is sick it will go hard and past all help;
but the traveller must set out ⟨now⟩: in time there will be no harm.

— And if three are ones, one a four, and the fifth a three: —
do not you do the deed you now set your hand to;
for now, while you are in sickness, the gods keep guard over you,
and they will loose your toil, and nothing bad shall be.

— And if three fours fall, and two ones: —
the Daimon will lead you on the road you set your hand to;
and smile-loving Aphrodite will send you toward the good;
with many fruits you shall walk, and with a fate unharmed.

— One dog, two falling as threes, and fours a pair: —
the deed you now set your hand to — go to it with courage; do it;
set your hand to the work, for the gods have shown fair oracles here;
and do not shrink from toil: for nothing bad shall come to you.

— And if there fall three ones and two sixes: —
the road you turn over in your mind — go upon it with courage;
god will grant everything: you shall accomplish all your heart commands;
and high-thundering Zeus shall stand beside you as saviour.

— A four, a three, and a six, and two ones: —
the deed you intend — do not hasten: the moment is not yet come;
and you who lie in sickness the gods stand ready to save;
and for him in another land, the god declares his road shall end.

— If one is the dog, and all the rest are fours in a row: —
now the daimon accomplishes all for you, and guides you aright;
you shall do everything after your mind — so wear yourself no longer;
you shall attain, blameless, all that you desire.

— One a one, one a six, two fours, and the fifth a three: —
what you are pondering shall not go according to your judgement;
for neither is it profitable for you to go abroad,
nor, in your buying, will you perceive what would profit.

— One a six, two threes, and fours twain: —
the one who hastens cannot seize what the Moment commands;
you have your gain, and god will loose you from every malice;
the deed is easy — but guard yourself against all that is wretched.

— Three fours, one a six, and the fifth a three: —
all that you wish you shall do; you shall find all that you ponder;
set your hand to it, stranger, taking courage: all stands ready;
the hidden you shall find, and the day of salvation comes to meet you.

— Three falling as threes, and two are sixes: this it declares: —
the deeds are fair, and this oracle bids you hasten;
you shall escape hard sickness, and master all;
and the god declares the wanderer in foreign lands shall come home.
